---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { business, url } from '../lib/site';
---

<Layout
  title="Our Menu Information, Images & Corrections | Bhuk Lagla"
  description="Who publishes Bhuk Lagla's menu guides, where dish information comes from, how AI-generated images are used, and how to request a correction."
>
  <section class="wrap prose section">
    <p class="eyebrow">About what you read here</p>
    <h1>
      Clear food information.
      <br />
      Honest context.
    </h1>
    <p>
      Bhuk Lagla publishes this website for people choosing vegetarian food in Sundargarh, Odisha.
      Our menu pages and guides help you compare dishes before opening Zomato or contacting the
      kitchen.
    </p>
    <p class="small-text">
      Published by Bhuk Lagla · Updated <time datetime="2026-10-17">17 October 2026</time>
    </p>
    <h2 id="sources">Where the information comes from</h2>
    <p>
      Dish names, selected ingredients and cooking-method descriptions come from the kitchen’s menu
      records and confirmed business information. The <a href={url('menu/')}>menu catalogue</a> is
      the source for our website comparisons and dish counts. It is not a live feed of platform
      availability.
    </p>
    <p>
      For current prices, portion choices, charges, delivery serviceability and offers, check Zomato
      for your location and account. Search snippets and AI answers may contain older information.
      An ingredient description is not a complete allergen declaration.
    </p>
    <h2 id="authorship">Who publishes the guides?</h2>
    <p>
      Articles are published under the Bhuk Lagla name and linked to{' '}
      <a href={url('about/')}>Our kitchen</a>. We use AI-assisted drafting and website tools to
      organise menu information into readable guides. A business byline identifies the publisher; it
      does not imply independent testing or a chef’s professional qualification.
    </p>
    <p>
      Comparisons explain differences in the named dishes. They do not claim a taste test, a
      customer survey, a nutrition study or a sales ranking. Event examples are planning examples
      unless a page explicitly describes a documented event. Where a guide uses an outside calendar
      or event source, it links to that source and identifies the relevant year.
    </p>
    <h2 id="images">About the food images</h2>
    <p>
      The current food images are <strong>AI-generated menu illustrations</strong> based on the dish
      descriptions. They are not camera photographs of individual orders or proof of portion size,
      preparation conditions or the exact appearance of a delivered dish. Actual presentation can
      vary. The mascot is brand artwork.
    </p>
    <h2 id="updates">Dates and updates</h2>
    <p>
      Article publication dates record when the guide was first published. An updated date is shown
      when the content is substantially revised. A dated festival guide describes that season; it is
      not a current-year event announcement. An edit date does not certify live stock or opening
      status.
    </p>
    <h2 id="corrections">Ask a question or request a correction</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${business.email}`}>{business.email}</a> or use the{' '}
      <a href={url('contact/?type=general')}>general enquiry form</a>. Include the page link and the
      detail that needs checking. For an existing Zomato order, use the help options within that
      order for platform payments, delivery and order status.
    </p>
    <p>
      For ingredients or a dietary restriction,{' '}
      <a href={url('answers/#allergies')}>ask the kitchen before ordering</a>. A vegetarian or
      egg-free label does not establish suitability for every allergy or diet.
    </p>
    <a class="button secondary" href={url('answers/')}>
      Read the food and ordering answers →
    </a>
  </section>
</Layout>
